1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The Blackfoot saw — lost
children.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
They call themselves Niitsitapi, “the
real people”. Today: Alberta and
Montana.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Tipis on the Great Plains. In a big
summer camp, a writer counted: one in
ten was painted.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The designs came in dreams and belong to
the owner. No one else may copy them.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,000
In spring, after the buffalo hunt,
children played in yellow calf robes.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Six poor children had none. The others
mocked them as “mangy old bulls”.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Ashamed to go home, they wandered the
prairie and were taken up into the sky.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
In autumn, when the calves turn brown,
they come back every night.

9
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Around 8 p.m. this month, the Lost
Children ride high in the south.

10
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Ancient Egypt: the star that woke the
Nile.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

